dominantWeightsBetti -- a hash table containing the dominant Schur functors of a Veronese embedding
***************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        dominantWeightsBetti(d,n,b)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * b, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, 

Description
===========

This function returns a hash table $H$ whose keys are pairs $(p,q)$ such that
the corresponding value $H#(p,q)$ is a list of the dominant weights appearing
in the Schur functor decomposition of $K_{p,q}(\mathbb{P}^n, d;b)$. The Schur
functors are recorded via the corresponding partitions. See Section 1.3 of
[BEGY].



+-------------------------------------+
