makeBettiTally -- converts a hash table representing a Betti table to a Betti tally
***********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        makeBettiTally(H)
  * Inputs:
      * H, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Betti tally: (Macaulay2Doc)BettiTally,, 

Description
===========

Given a hash table $H$ whose keys are pairs of integers $(p,q)$ this function
presents the data in the Betti tally format. For instance, combining this with
the *note totalBetti: totalBetti, function reproduces the standard Betti table.
By contrast, combining this with the numRepsBetti function produces a table
where the entry in position $(p,q)$ is the number of Schur functors in the
representation corresponding to that Betti table entry.

+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : H = totalBetti(3,2,0);            |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : makeBettiTally H                  |
|                                       |
|            0  1   2   3   4   5  6 7  |
|o2 = total: 1 27 105 189 189 105 27 1  |
|         0: 1  .   .   .   .   .  . .  |
|         1: . 27 105 189 189 105 27 .  |
|         2: .  .   .   .   .   .  . 1  |
|                                       |
|o2 : BettiTally                        |
+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : makeBettiTally numRepsBetti(3,2,0)|
|                                       |
|            0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7            |
|o3 = total: 1 1 4 7 7 4 1 1            |
|         0: 1 . . . . . . .            |
|         1: . 1 4 7 7 4 1 .            |
|         2: . . . . . . . 1            |
|                                       |
|o3 : BettiTally                        |
+---------------------------------------+

