multiBetti -- a hash table containing the multigraded Betti numbers of a Veronese embedding
*******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        multiBetti(d,n,b)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * b, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, 

Description
===========

This function returns a hash table $H$ containing the multigraded Betti numbers
for $\mathcal{O}(b)$ on $\mathbb{P}^{n}$ under the embedding by $d$-fold
Veronese embedding given by $\mathcal{O}(d)$. The keys of the returned hash
table $H$ are pairs $(p,q)$ where $H#(p,q)$ gives the the multigraded Betti
decomposition of $K_{p,q}(\mathbb{P}^n, d;b)$. We record the multigraded Betti
numbers via a multigraded Hilbert series. See Section 1.1 of [BEGY] for a more
precise description of the multigraded Betti numbers of a Veronese embedding.

Note that the output of this function is sometimes enormous and so can take a
long time to print on the screen.

